{
  "id": "response-has-no-msg-attribute-setattr-silently-succeeds",
  "title": "Response has no `msg` attribute: setattr silently succeeds",
  "kind": "gotcha",
  "answers": [
    "Why did the reason phrase edit have no effect?",
    "Is Response.msg a real field?"
  ],
  "body": "`mitmproxy/http.py` Response exposes `reason` (property/setter), not `msg`. A `setattr(response, \"msg\", v)` in `app.py` just creates a stray attribute, so tests asserting `f.response.msg` pass without proving anything. When adding update keys in the web app handler, assert on the real property (e.g. `reason`).",
  "applies": "Web API flow update handler for response fields; setattr-based branches on Python objects without __slots__.",
